---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/docs.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base
	title="Budget Insights | Actual Budget Tweaks"
	description="Month summary, template previews and breakdowns in the Actual Budget Tweaks side panel."
>
	<main class="docs center">
		<header class="docs__header stack stack--sm">
			<a href="/guides" class="docs__back">Back to guides</a>
			<h1>Budget Insights</h1>
			<p class="docs__lead">
				Budget Insights adds a side panel to the budget page with a month summary, a preview of your
				budget templates, and a list of what each change moved. It works with envelope budgeting.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Open the panel</h2>
			<ol>
				<li>Turn on Budget Insights in Tweaks.</li>
				<li>Click <strong>Insights</strong> on the budget page.</li>
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Check the month</h2>
			<p>The Overview tab follows the month you have open.</p>
			<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--card">
				<img
					src={`${base}images/guides/insights-overview.png`}
					width="350"
					height="931"
					alt="The Overview tab, with overspent categories, the month's spending, next month's shortfall, unfunded goals and a chart of spent against budgeted"
				/>
			</div>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Overspent</strong> appears when any category is below zero.</li>
				<li><strong>This Month</strong> shows where your available funds went.</li>
				<li><strong>Next Month</strong> compares money held for next month with what it needs.</li>
				<li><strong>Goals to Fund</strong> lists categories whose templates aren't met yet.</li>
				<li><strong>Spent vs Budgeted</strong> covers the last six months.</li>
				<li><strong>Coming Up</strong> lists scheduled transactions for the next 30 days.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Next Month measures against your goal templates. To use your recent average spending
				instead, change the Next Month Target setting in Tweaks.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Preview your templates</h2>
			<p>The Priority plan tab shows how far your available money goes, one priority at a time.</p>
						<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--card">
				<img
					src={`${base}images/guides/insights-priority.png`}
					width="350"
					height="640"
					alt="The Priority plan tab, with priorities 0 and 1 funded, priority 2 partly funded, and priorities 3 and 4 unfunded"
				/>
			</div>
			<p>Priorities are funded in order, lowest number first.</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Funded priorities get everything they asked for.</li>
				<li>The partly funded priority is where the money runs out.</li>
				<li>Unfunded priorities come after it and get nothing.</li>
				<li><strong>Gap remaining</strong> is how much more you need to fund everything.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>This tab is a preview and doesn't change your budget.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Apply templates and see what moved</h2>
			<ol>
				<li>Click <strong>Apply</strong> on the Overview tab.</li>
				<li>Open the Breakdown tab to see what each priority and category received.</li>
			</ol>
			<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--card">
				<img
					src={`${base}images/guides/insights-breakdown.png`}
					width="350"
					height="640"
					alt="The Breakdown tab listing the amount each priority and category received after applying templates"
				/>
			</div>
			<p>To reverse it, use Actual's undo.</p>
		</section>
	</main>
</Base>
